equirements Fees and Costs Scholarships and Discounts Inbound student mobility Outbound student mobility Accommodation Visa and medical insurance Life in Budapest and Hungary Contact us University About Corvinus Maecenas Universitatis Corvini Foundation Organisation Institutes Departments Senate, University Committees Campuses Gellért Campus Corvinus Doctoral Schools Whistleblowing reports Regulations, Provisions, Directives Non-Regulatory Documents Ethics, Responsibility, Sustainability Corporate partners Contact Research Corvinus Research Neuro- and Digital Marketing Research Center (NEDIMARC) Corvinus Institute for Advanced Studies Regional Centre for Energy Policy Research Research Centres CCL at Corvinus University University Library University Archives Research and development projects Scientific Students’ Associations Conference (TDK) Journals, working papers, repositories Corvinus Science Shop Students For Freshers International and Administrative Student Services MyCorvinus Navigator Makerspace Media Studio Scholarship Student’s Union Doctoral Student Council Digital advances at Corvinus Students Satisfaction Evaluation Using Artificial Intelligence For our current students Accommodation Student Organisations IT Services Student support services Career support Sport and health Schedule of the Academic Year Subjects Alumni News News Events Success Stories Media Library International Blog Other Menus Corvinus Institute for Advanced Studies (CIAS) Research Centers ANETI Lab Business Ethics Center Corvinus Center for Operations Research Center for Cognitive Infocommunications Center for Collective Learning Center for Contemporary Asia Studies Ecological Economics Research Center Family, Household and Economy Regional Centre for Energy Policy Research Research Projects Encyclopedia of Hungarian Philosophy Transportation networks in dynamic urban structures CIAS Inn Corvinus Institute for Advanced Studies (CIAS) Research Centers ANETI Lab Business Ethics Center Corvinus Center for Operations Research Center for Cognitive Infocommunications Center for Collective Learning Center for Contemporary Asia Studies Ecological Economics Research Center Family, Household and Economy Regional Centre for Energy Policy Research Research Projects Encyclopedia of Hungarian Philosophy Transportation networks in dynamic urban structures CIAS Inn Regional Centre for Energy Policy Research About the Center The Regional Centre for Energy Policy Research (REKK) is an independent research institution dedicated to the fields of energy, water, and environmental economics. With a mission to foster economically efficient and environmentally sustainable market operations, REKK provides high-quality research, consultancy, and knowledge dissemination services. Its vision is to shape regulatory frameworks and corporate strategies at both national and international levels, thereby contributing to well-functioning and future-proof energy and environmental sectors. REKK’s primary goal is to support evidence-based policy-making and business decision-making through rigorous, policy-relevant analysis grounded in economic theory and empirical research. Over the past two decades, REKK has conducted extensive research and consultancy work in a wide range of areas. These include electricity and natural gas markets—particularly in relation to network regulation and large consumer interests—along with the district heating sector, where research focuses on service regulation and corporate strategy. In the field of water economics, REKK addresses issues such as utility management, catchment area governance, and flood risk management. The centre also examines renewable energy deployment, its economic impacts, and long-term policy support, while its work on decarbonisation includes emissions trading systems and national energy and climate planning. Additionally, REKK engages in research on transport, energy use in SMEs, and building energy efficiency, reflecting its broad commitment to sustainable development across interconnected sectors. Further Information Head of Research Center Szabó László lszabo@uni-corvinus.hu +36 1 482 5153 • Ext: 5153 E épület, 117 Tudományos főmunkatárs (REKK) / Senior Research Fellow Regional Center for Energy Policy Research) Rektori Szervezet / Kutatási és akadémiai közösségért felelős rh. / Corvinus Institute for Advanced Studies / // Regionális Energiagazdasági Kutatóközpont CV Scholar MTMT Other 1 Other 2 Members of Research Center Mezősi András andras.mezosi@uni-corvinus.hu +36 1 482 5153 • Ext: 5153 E épület, 117 Tudományos főmunkatárs / Senior Research Fellow Rektori Szervezet / Regionális Energiagazdasági Kutatóközpont CV LinkedIn Scholar MTMT Rácz Viktor +36 1 482 5153 • Ext: 5153 E épület, 117 Szajkó Gabriella gabriella.pal@uni-corvinus.hu +36 1 482 5153 • Ext: 5153 E épület, 117 Kutató / Researcher Rektori Szervezet / Regionális Energiagazdasági Kutatóközpont CV Takácsné Tóth Borbála borbala.toth@uni-corvinus.hu +36 20 354 4270 E épület, 117 Tudományos munkatárs / Research Fellow Rektori Szervezet / Regionális Energiagazdasági Kutatóközpont CV MTMT Other 1 Mészégetőné Keszthelyi Andrea andrea.keszthelyi@uni-corvinus.hu +36 1 482 5153 • Ext: 5153 E épület, 117 Irodavezető / Head of Office Rektori Szervezet / Regionális Energiagazdasági Kutatóközpont Copied to clipboard Manage consent Contact Us Telephone: +36 1 482 5000 Do you have questions about the admissions? Academic Contacts For current students HUB Press: press@uni-corvinus.hu Useful information Opening Hours House Rules Public Data Career at Corvinus Design Elements RRF Public data Follow us Facebook LinkedIn Youtube Instagram TikTok X International accreditations Main international memberships Cookie & Data Management Settings Policy © Corvinus University of Budapest ×"
